{"title":"A Constellation of Amazements: An Illustrated Love Letter to the Joy of Collecting Things","link":"https://www.themarginalian.org/2026/10/06/these-are-my-rocks/","date":1791318722000,"content":"<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/These-Are-Rocks-Bethan-Woollvin/dp/1836004664/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" width=\"320\" height=\"376\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks.jpg?fit=320%2C376&amp;ssl=1\" alt=\"A Constellation of Amazements: An Illustrated Love Letter to the Joy of Collecting Things\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks.jpg?w=1275&amp;ssl=1 1275w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks.jpg?resize=320%2C376&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks.jpg?resize=600%2C706&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks.jpg?resize=240%2C282&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks.jpg?resize=768%2C904&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p><p>We are hunter-gatherers with a capacity for amazement, wired to search for an organizing principle by which to contain the chaos of reality. We organize what we find into categories and hierarchies, hovering over which is one of the strangest things about being human: preference. How odd to have a strong feeling about a color or an object or a sequence of chords. And yet our preferences are how we sculpt the self from the monolith of the species. </p>\n<p>Preference taken to its highest form touches amazement — the glad disbelief that something so personally relevant and rapturous could exist amid the impersonal allness of all there is. One of the most moving things about us, and one of the most felicitous things about being alive together, is that we get to share our amazements. A collection — be it of rocks or vinyl records or facts about the Moon — is a constellation of amazements in the sky of one mind that can light up another with its loveliness, its strangeness, its sheer delight. </p>\n<p>Once, visiting Maurice Sendak’s farmhouse, I was struck by the ample shelves and antique medicine cabinets lined with Mickey Mouse figurines of every possible variety. I don’t have a strong feeling about Mickey Mouse, but Sendak’s tender and meticulous preference gave me inordinate delight. After all, if <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2024/11/29/sandol-stoddard-particular-cat/\">to love is to cherish the particular in a person</a>, then to collect particulars is a practice of loving the world. </p>\n<p>That is what Bethan Woollvin celebrates in the brightly delightful <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/These-Are-Rocks-Bethan-Woollvin/dp/1836004664/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><strong><em>These Are My Rocks: A Story About Collecting</em></strong></a> (<a href=\"https://search.worldcat.org/title/1484506626\" target=\"_blank\"><em>public library</em></a>).</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/These-Are-Rocks-Bethan-Woollvin/dp/1836004664/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks12.jpg?resize=680%2C691&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"691\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks12.jpg?w=750&amp;ssl=1 750w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks12.jpg?resize=320%2C325&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks12.jpg?resize=600%2C610&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks12.jpg?resize=240%2C244&amp;ssl=1 240w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/These-Are-Rocks-Bethan-Woollvin/dp/1836004664/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks10.jpg?resize=680%2C618&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"618\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks10.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks10.jpg?resize=320%2C291&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks10.jpg?resize=600%2C546&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks10.jpg?resize=240%2C218&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks10.jpg?resize=768%2C698&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/These-Are-Rocks-Bethan-Woollvin/dp/1836004664/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks2.jpg?resize=680%2C574&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"574\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks2.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks2.jpg?resize=320%2C270&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks2.jpg?resize=600%2C507&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks2.jpg?resize=240%2C203&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks2.jpg?resize=768%2C648&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p>Page by page, collection by collection — rocks, pointy things, broken things, invisible things, banana jokes — the essence of collecting, this strange impulse humans share with almost no other animal (except perhaps <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2023/10/29/bowerbird/\">the bowerbird</a>), is revealed: to find things and “be amazed by what you find.”</p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/These-Are-Rocks-Bethan-Woollvin/dp/1836004664/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks4.jpg?resize=680%2C716&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"716\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks4.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks4.jpg?resize=320%2C337&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks4.jpg?resize=600%2C632&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks4.jpg?resize=240%2C253&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks4.jpg?resize=768%2C809&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/These-Are-Rocks-Bethan-Woollvin/dp/1836004664/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks13.jpg?resize=680%2C399&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"399\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks13.jpg?w=1500&amp;ssl=1 1500w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks13.jpg?resize=320%2C188&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks13.jpg?resize=600%2C352&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks13.jpg?resize=240%2C141&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks13.jpg?resize=768%2C451&amp;ssl=1 768w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks13.jpg?w=1360&amp;ssl=1 1360w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/These-Are-Rocks-Bethan-Woollvin/dp/1836004664/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks9.jpg?resize=680%2C805&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"805\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks9.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks9.jpg?resize=320%2C379&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks9.jpg?resize=600%2C710&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks9.jpg?resize=240%2C284&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks9.jpg?resize=768%2C909&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/These-Are-Rocks-Bethan-Woollvin/dp/1836004664/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks3.jpg?resize=680%2C534&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"534\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks3.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks3.jpg?resize=320%2C251&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks3.jpg?resize=600%2C471&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks3.jpg?resize=240%2C188&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks3.jpg?resize=768%2C603&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/These-Are-Rocks-Bethan-Woollvin/dp/1836004664/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks5.jpg?resize=680%2C526&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"526\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks5.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks5.jpg?resize=320%2C248&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks5.jpg?resize=600%2C465&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks5.jpg?resize=240%2C186&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks5.jpg?resize=768%2C595&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/These-Are-Rocks-Bethan-Woollvin/dp/1836004664/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks11.jpg?resize=680%2C561&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"561\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks11.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks11.jpg?resize=320%2C264&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks11.jpg?resize=600%2C495&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks11.jpg?resize=240%2C198&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks11.jpg?resize=768%2C634&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/These-Are-Rocks-Bethan-Woollvin/dp/1836004664/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><img loading=\"lazy\" src=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks14.jpg?resize=680%2C670&amp;ssl=1\" width=\"680\" height=\"670\" srcset=\"https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks14.jpg?w=1200&amp;ssl=1 1200w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks14.jpg?resize=320%2C315&amp;ssl=1 320w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks14.jpg?resize=600%2C592&amp;ssl=1 600w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks14.jpg?resize=240%2C237&amp;ssl=1 240w, https://i0.wp.com/www.themarginalian.org/wp-content/uploads/2026/10/thesearemyrocks14.jpg?resize=768%2C757&amp;ssl=1 768w\" /></a></p>\n<p>For a perfect counterpart, complement <a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/These-Are-Rocks-Bethan-Woollvin/dp/1836004664/?tag=braipick-20\" target=\"_blank\"><strong><em>These Are My Rocks</em></strong></a> with Finnish author and artist Maija Hurme’s <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2026/08/21/odds-and-ends-maija-hurme/\"><em>Odds and Ends</em></a> — an illustrated love letter to the opposite of collecting: the loveliness of letting things go. </p>\n<hr /><h3>donating = loving</h3><p>For seventeen years, I have been spending hundreds of hours and thousands of dollars each month composing <em>The Marginalian</em> (which <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/2021/10/22/brain-pickings-becoming-the-marginalian/\">bore the outgrown name <em>Brain Pickings</em></a> for its first fifteen years). It has remained free and ad-free and alive thanks to patronage from readers. I have no staff, no interns, no assistant — a thoroughly one-woman labor of love that is also my life and my livelihood. If this labor makes your own life more livable in any way, please consider lending a helping hand with a <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/donate/\">donation</a>. Your support makes all the difference.</p>\n\n<hr />\n\n<h3>newsletter</h3>\n<p><em>The Marginalian</em> has a free weekly newsletter. It comes out on Sundays and offers the week’s most inspiring reading. Here’s <a href=\"https://mailchi.mp/brainpickings/janna-levin-rebecca-elson-anne-lamott-james-gleick\">what to expect</a>. Like? <a href=\"https://www.themarginalian.org/newsletter/\">Sign up.</a></p>","author":"Maria Popova","siteTitle":"The Marginalian","siteHash":"052ac1be0de11784b9ef27664fbcf33da8263d0e7cb9c6e601ccd959f2d3aa78","entryHash":"ffe6ebc12c95ea867796c0ed09546ba29e2769211f302fd92dd6254cbb76600a","category":"Sites"}